# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__/**
.pytest_cache/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# ── Julia ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Manifest.toml IS committed (root + experiments/) — it is the reproducibility record.
*.jl.cov
*.jl.*.cov
*.jl.mem
/docs/build/

# ── Reference PDFs (large; not redistributable) ───────────────────────────────
*.pdf

# ── Generated figure outputs (regenerate via the plotting scripts) ────────────
figures/
*.png
*.svg

# ── Docs / session logs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Working notes stay LOCAL. Do not commit docs unless explicitly asked.
docs/

# ── OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store

# ── Artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The kernels the DEFAULT config and the tests need are committed: `tables.json`
# (noise-free) and `tables_noisy_gaussian0.7.json` (the shipped thruster law). They are the
# model's measured input (~24 KB each), carry their own provenance, and reviewing a diff in
# one is how a re-measurement gets noticed.
#
# The nav-keyed artifacts are NOT committed. `experiments/sweep.jl` measures one per swept
# navigation level on demand, so there is no fixed set to ship, and a sweep can generate a
# dozen.
artifacts/tables*_nav*.json
#
# Everything else here is a build product, reproducible from those kernels plus the config:
#   solver/   SARSOP's own .out policies and .pomdpx models (tens of MB per solve)
#   sweeps/   per-rollout checkpoints, re-runnable via experiments/sweep.jl
#   *.log     run logs
# A re-solve rewrites almost every byte, so committing them would add unreclaimable history.
artifacts/solver/
artifacts/sweeps/
artifacts/*.log
# Per-level run logs from experiments/cluster/run_sweep.sh.
logs/
# The dense-T JSON policy archive, superseded by SARSOP's .out (see src/export.jl). ~1.6 GB
# each at |S| = 5627.
artifacts/policy.json
artifacts/policy_*

# Claude Code project instructions (local only)
CLAUDE.md
claude.md

# Local verification/comparison harnesses (not committed)
scratch/

# SARSOP.jl defaults to writing these into the WORKING directory; artifacts/solver/ is
# where the scripts redirect them.
*.pomdpx
*.out
